From ac2c19fa0a955fc705af66337bee22ffde0fd31b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 20:06:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 9/9] engines: register sshfs on macOS again

fa572d7("instantiate engines only in supported platforms",Nov 2018)
replaced one flat engine list with a list per platform and sshfs did not
make it into the macOS branch,while Windows and Linux both kept it.  So
the backend is unreachable there however it is installed.

Nothing suggests it was meant to go: sshfs::_setOptions() still picks a
macOS specific unmount command,

    if( utility::platformIsOSX() ){
            s.unMountCommand = QStringList{ "umount","%{mountPoint}" } ;
    }

which has been dead code since that commit.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CHd6nUCuxo4ac7p7eGehu2
---
 src/engines.cpp | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/engines.cpp b/src/engines.cpp
index dbdebe5..314338d 100644
--- a/src/engines.cpp
+++ b/src/engines.cpp
@@ -1935,6 +1935,7 @@ engines::engines()
 		m_backends.emplace_back( std::make_unique< cryfs >() ) ;
 		m_backends.emplace_back( std::make_unique< gocryptfs >() ) ;
 		m_backends.emplace_back( std::make_unique< encfs >() ) ;
+		m_backends.emplace_back( std::make_unique< sshfs >() ) ;
 
 	}else if( utility::platformIsFlatPak() ){
 
